cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the AI Governance Standards Baseline dataset, please cite Dr Michelle O'Rourke for this dataset release and the originating authority for any external source or clause relied upon."
title: "AI Governance Standards Baseline"
type: dataset
version: "0.0.1"
date-released: "2026-08-24"
authors:
  - family-names: "O'Rourke"
    given-names: "Michelle"
    name-particle: "Dr"
abstract: >
  The AI Governance Standards Baseline is a machine-readable VIGIL dataset of
  governance-source metadata and clause/control records drawn from laws,
  standards, frameworks and technical guidance relevant to AI governance. It
  provides source-level public summaries, AI-governance relevance themes,
  lifecycle applicability, substantive review dates and clause-level analytical
  requirement records where available.
keywords:
  - "AI governance"
  - "AI standards"
  - "AI regulation"
  - "governance requirements"
  - "assurance"
  - "risk management"
  - "VIGIL"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CAM-Initiative/Vigil"
url: "https://www.cam-initiative.org/observatory/knowledge-base/standards-sources"
license: "CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0"
identifiers:
  - type: "url"
    value: "https://github.com/CAM-Initiative/Vigil/tree/main/vigil/external_requirements"
notes: >
  Dataset version 0.0.1. Review-freshness-only updates may regenerate package
  artefacts without incrementing the semantic dataset version; package build
  metadata and integrity hashes are recorded in the accompanying manifest.
